      "That enclosed bowl creates the highest year-round density of large mammals in East Africa: roughly 25,000 resident animals live inside the crater rim, including one of northern Tanzania's very few reliable populations of endangered black rhinos, thick-maned male lions, spotted hyena clans, golden jackals, old bull elephants with heavy ivory, Cape buffalo, zebra, wildebeest, and hippos. Notably absent are giraffes and impala, whose long legs struggle with the steep rocky descent walls.",
